<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1898</h1><p class="ref-lede">1898 in world history: 39 events, 30 births, 18 deaths, 4 works, 13 states founded and 8 that came to an end. 863 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1894">1894</a><a href="/years/1895">1895</a><a href="/years/1896">1896</a><a href="/years/1897">1897</a><a href="/years/1898" aria-current="page">1898</a><a href="/years/1899">1899</a><a href="/years/1900">1900</a><a href="/years/1901">1901</a><a href="/years/1902">1902</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-13">13 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Émile Zola publishes 'J'accuse...!'</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Zola's open letter in L'Aurore accused the French army of convicting the Jewish officer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-dreyfus">Alfred Dreyfus</a> wrongly and covering up the truth. It turned the Dreyfus affair into a national crisis.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-15">15 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">USS Maine explodes in Havana harbour</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">An explosion sank the American battleship, killing some 260 men. The cause is still debated, but US newspapers blamed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, and the cry 'Remember the Maine' helped bring war in April.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-12">12 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Emilio Aguinaldo declares Philippine independence</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kawit">Kawit</a>, Cavite, revolutionaries proclaimed independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> annexed the islands instead, and full independence came only in 1946.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-7">7 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">President McKinley signs the resolution annexing Hawaii</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">McKinley signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newlands-resolution">Newlands Resolution</a>, annexing the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a> five years after American businessmen had overthrown Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lili-uokalani">Liliuokalani</a>. Hawaii became a US territory and, in 1959, the 50th state.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/manila" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manila.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-13">13 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">US forces take Manila from Spain</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">American troops occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> after a largely staged battle with the Spanish garrison, unaware that a peace protocol had been signed the day before. The US went on to annex the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-days-reform" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hundred-days-reform.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-21">21 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Empress Dowager Cixi seizes power and ends the Hundred Days' Reform</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empress-dowager-cixi">Cixi</a>'s seizure of power ended a reform movement begun on 11 June that had sought to modernise <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s institutions after its defeat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-sino-japanese-war">First Sino-Japanese War</a>. Though brief, it inspired many of the New Policies reforms launched after 1901.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empress-dowager-cixi">Empress Dowager Cixi</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-days-reform">Hundred Days' Reform</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-10">10 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">White supremacists overthrow the elected government of Wilmington</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">White supremacists in Wilmington, North Carolina, massacred black residents and overthrew the city's elected government, the only such coup against a municipal government in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> history. Studies since 2016 have called it terrorism.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/paris" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paris.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-21">21 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Curies identify radium</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Working in a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> shed, Marie and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pierre-curie">Pierre Curie</a> detected a new, intensely radioactive element in pitchblende, announced days later as radium. Isolating it took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marie-curie">Marie Curie</a> another twelve years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-26">26 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Curies announce the discovery of radium</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A paper presented to the French Academy of Sciences announced radium, a new element found in pitchblende by Marie and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pierre-curie">Pierre Curie</a> with Gustave Bémont. It later proved vital in early cancer treatment.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spanish-american-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">War</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-war">Spanish–American War</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Spanish–American War was fought in 1898 between Spain and the United States, arising from the Cuban struggle for independence.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1898" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1898.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1898">Treaty of Paris (1898)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Paris of December 1898 ended the Spanish–American War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-manila-bay" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-manila-bay.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-manila-bay">Battle of Manila Bay</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Manila Bay was fought on 1 May 1898, at the start of the Spanish–American War, when the US Asiatic Squadron under Commodore George Dewey destroyed the Spanish Pacific squadron of Admiral Patricio Montojo off Cavite in the Philippines.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-santiago-de-cuba" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-santiago-de-cuba.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-santiago-de-cuba">Battle of Santiago de Cuba</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Santiago de Cuba was a naval battle fought on 3 July 1898 during the Spanish–American War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/anglo-french-convention-of-1898">Anglo-French Convention of 1898</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Anglo-French Convention of 1898 was an agreement signed in Paris on 14 June 1898 that settled the frontier between British and French territories in West Africa, especially along the Niger.</p></div></li></ol></section>
