<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/darfur-sultanate"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Darfur%20Sultanate.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Darfur Sultanate</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Ali Dinar returns to El Fasher and restores the sultanate</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/german-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/German%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>German Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The first Naval Law launches Tirpitz's challenge to British sea power</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/spanish-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Spanish%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Spanish Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Defeat by the United States strips Spain of Cuba, Puerto Rico and the Philippines</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/congo-free-state"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Congo%20Free%20State.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Congo Free State</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Matadi–Léopoldville railway is completed</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/direct-democracy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Direct%20democracy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Direct democracy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">South Dakota becomes the first US state to adopt the initiative and the referendum</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/dong-son-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dong%20Son%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dong Son culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Austrian archaeologist Franz Heger, creator of a classification of bronze drums, turns to the drums</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/chinese-folk-religion"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Chinese%20folk%20religion.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Chinese folk religion</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Kang Youwei persuades the emperor to order temples that perform no state sacrifices turned into schools; the confiscations are soon reversed</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/lili-uokalani"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Lili%CA%BBuokalani.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Liliʻuokalani</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Hawaiʻi is annexed by the United States through the Newlands Resolution; she boycotts the ceremony of 12 August and publishes her memoir</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/chamorro-people"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Chamorro%20people.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Chamorro people</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The United States captured Guam during the Spanish–American War</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/otto-von-bismarck"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Otto%20von%20Bismarck.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Otto von Bismarck</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Dies at Friedrichsruh, where he is entombed in the Bismarck Mausoleum</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/manila"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Manila.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Manila</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Spain cedes the Philippines to the United States after the Battle of Manila</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/hong-kong"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hong%20Kong.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hong Kong</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Britain obtains a 99-year lease of the New Territories</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/khartoum"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Khartoum.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Khartoum</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Anglo-Egyptian forces reoccupy the city, which becomes the capital of Anglo-Egyptian Sudan</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/havana"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Havana.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Havana</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Spain relinquishes sovereignty over Cuba after the sinking of the USS Maine in Havana harbour</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/honolulu"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Honolulu.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Honolulu</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The United States annexes Hawaii</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/marie-curie"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Marie%20Curie.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Marie Curie</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Announces polonium with Pierre in July and radium in December, and coins the word radioactivity</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/empress-dowager-cixi"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Empress%20Dowager%20Cixi.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Empress Dowager Cixi</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">She ends the Hundred Days' Reform and confines the Guangxu Emperor to Ocean Terrace</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/hundred-days-reform"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hundred%20Days'%20Reform.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hundred Days' Reform</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Guangxu Emperor begins to issue the reform edicts, on 11 June</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/hundred-days-reform"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hundred%20Days'%20Reform.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hundred Days' Reform</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Empress Dowager Cixi stages a coup, places the emperor under house arrest and orders the leading reformers executed</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/neoliberalism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Neoliberalism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Neoliberalism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The French economist Charles Gide uses the term in English to describe the beliefs of the Italian economist Maffeo Pantaleoni</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/manifest-destiny"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Manifest%20destiny.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Manifest destiny</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">William McKinley annexes Hawaii and the Spanish–American War brings the Philippines, Puerto Rico and Guam</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/santeria"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Santer%C3%ADa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Santería</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Cuba becomes an independent republic whose constitution enshrines freedom of religion</span></li></ul></section>
